@nzakas Of course it should:

``` js
f();
// ...
export default function f(){}
```

This is exactly the kind of thing this rule is meant to avoid. What we were discussing is whether it should apply to an unnamed default export.

The rule isn't about enforcing a name or not, it's about the stylistic preference between these:

``` js
function foo() {}
var foo = function(){};
```

Forcing people to put parentheses around or name a default exported function doesn't seem remotely related to that.
